<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net"><diagram name="Data Model" id="learn-data"><mxGraphModel dx="2400" dy="2000" grid="1" gridSize="10" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2400" pageHeight="2000" background="#ffffff"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="t" value="ONLINE LEARNING PLATFORM - Data Model (PostgreSQL Sharded + S3 Video + Kafka + Elasticsearch + Redis)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;fontSize=20;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1a237e" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="20" width="2280" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="postgresTitle" value="POSTGRESQL SCHEMAS (Course DB + Progress DB Sharded by user_id + Payment DB)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;fillColor=#f3e5f5;align=left;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;rounded=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="80" width="2280" height="25" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="courseTable" value="TABLE: courses&#10;&#10;course_id PK&#10;owner_instructor_id FK&#10;title, description&#10;category_id, level (BEGINNER/&#10;  INTERMEDIATE/ADVANCED)&#10;thumbnail_url&#10;status (DRAFT/IN_REVIEW/&#10;  PUBLISHED/REJECTED/ARCHIVED)&#10;students_enrolled (counter,&#10;  incremented on enrollment event)&#10;rating DECIMAL(3,2)&#10;  (updated async from reviews)&#10;&#10;INDEXES:&#10;INDEX (category, rating)&#10;INDEX (instructor_id, created_at)&#10;INDEX (published_status)&#10;&#10;TABLE: course_pricing&#10;course_id PK/FK&#10;price_amount, currency&#10;&#10;TABLE: course_stats (denormalized)&#10;course_id, avg_rating,&#10;total_reviews, enrolled,&#10;completion_rate&#10;Updated async via Kafka&#10;Aggregator CDC pipeline&#10;Avoids COUNT() on hot&#10;listing queries" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="120" width="360" height="500" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="enrollmentTable" value="TABLE: enrollments&#10;&#10;enrollment_id PK&#10;user_id, course_id&#10;owner_instructor_id&#10;enrolled_at DATETIME&#10;completion_status DECIMAL(5,2)&#10;payment_id&#10;metadata&#10;&#10;UNIQUE(user_id, course_id)&#10;  Database-level safety net&#10;  against enrollment race&#10;&#10;INDEXES:&#10;UNIQUE INDEX (user_id, course_id)&#10;INDEX (user_id, enrolled_at)&#10;&#10;PERMANENT RECORD:&#10;Never deleted, even on refund&#10;Historical proof of enrollment&#10;&#10;TABLE: access (SEPARATE FROM ENROLLMENT)&#10;access_id PK&#10;user_id, course_id&#10;scope_type (LIFETIME/SUBSCRIPTION)&#10;status (ACTIVE/REVOKED/EXPIRED)&#10;purchase_date&#10;&#10;Permission Sync Svc updates:&#10;payment.completed → ACTIVE&#10;refund.issued (30-day) → REVOKED&#10;subscription.expired → EXPIRED&#10;&#10;Video Playback checks Access&#10;NOT Enrollments before streaming" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffebee;strokeColor=#c62828;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="440" y="120" width="380" height="500" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="progressTable" value="TABLE: progress (SHARDED BY user_id)&#10;&#10;PRIMARY KEY (user_id, course_id, lesson_id)&#10;video_id (if lesson is video)&#10;duration_sec&#10;last_position_sec&#10;  (resume point, always latest sent)&#10;max_position_sec&#10;  (farthest watched, GREATEST&#10;   never decreases on rewind,&#10;   used for completion check)&#10;completed (bool)&#10;metadata&#10;&#10;COMPLETION LOGIC:&#10;IF max_position_sec &gt;=&#10;   duration_sec × 0.95 (95%)&#10;THEN status=COMPLETED&#10;UPDATE enrollments SET&#10;  completion_status =&#10;  (completed_lessons/total)×100&#10;&#10;WHY SHARD BY user_id:&#10;User's all progress rows on same&#10;shard, enables fast range queries&#10;for a single user's course view&#10;&#10;TABLE: quiz_attempts&#10;attempt_id PK&#10;quiz_id, user_id&#10;status (IN_PROGRESS/COMPLETED)&#10;start_time, attempt_number&#10;score, percentage, passed&#10;completed_at&#10;&#10;Acts as sealed exam envelope:&#10;prevents 2 simultaneous attempts,&#10;enforces countdown timer via&#10;start_time, auto-submits at&#10;time_limit expiry" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1bee7;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="840" y="120" width="380" height="500" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="paymentTable" value="TABLE: payments (SHARDED BY created_at)&#10;&#10;payment_id PK&#10;user_id, course_id&#10;amount DECIMAL&#10;status (PENDING/COMPLETED/&#10;  FAILED/REFUNDED)&#10;stripe_payment_id&#10;enrollment_request_id&#10;  (CLIENT-GENERATED idempotency key,&#10;   server never generates this)&#10;&#10;IDEMPOTENCY (5 layers):&#10;1. Client enrollmentRequestId&#10;   → Stripe dedupes PaymentIntent&#10;2. Kafka consumer DB check&#10;   before INSERT enrollment&#10;3. UNIQUE(user_id,course_id)&#10;   safety net&#10;4. Polling backup every 5 min&#10;   for lost webhooks&#10;5. All paths converge to same&#10;   idempotent outcome&#10;&#10;TABLE: orders&#10;order_id PK, user_id&#10;currency, amount_total&#10;status, metadata&#10;&#10;WHY SHARD BY created_at:&#10;Time-based for historical&#10;financial reporting queries" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1240" y="120" width="380" height="500" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="quizTable" value="TABLE: quizzes&#10;&#10;quiz_id PK, course_id, lesson_id&#10;title, pass_score (70%)&#10;time_limit (600s)&#10;attempts_allowed (3)&#10;&#10;TABLE: questions&#10;question_id PK, quiz_id&#10;type (MCQ_SINGLE/MULTI_SELECT/&#10;  FILL/SELECT/TRUE_FALSE/TEXT)&#10;options JSON&#10;correct_answer, points&#10;status, metadata&#10;&#10;AUTO-GRADE LOGIC:&#10;FOR EACH answer:&#10;  IF answer==correct_answer&#10;    score += points&#10;percentage = (score/total)×100&#10;passed = percentage &gt;= 70&#10;&#10;TABLE: certificates&#10;certificate_id PK&#10;user_id, course_id&#10;issued_at, s3_url&#10;&#10;IDEMPOTENCY GUARD:&#10;SELECT COUNT(*) FROM certificates&#10;WHERE user_id=? AND course_id=?&#10;count &gt; 0 → SKIP re-issue&#10;on Kafka retry/redelivery&#10;&#10;TABLE: reviews&#10;review_id, user_id, course_id&#10;rating (1-5), comment&#10;helpful_votes&#10;UNIQUE(user_id, course_id)&#10;  one review per enrolled student" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1bee7;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1640" y="120" width="380" height="500" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="kafkaTitle" value="KAFKA TOPICS (Event-Driven Async Processing)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#ef6c00;fillColor=#fff3e0;align=left;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;rounded=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="650" width="1160" height="25" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="kafkaVideo" value="TOPIC: video.uploaded&#10;&#10;PRODUCER: Lambda (S3 event trigger)&#10;CONSUMER: Video Transcode Worker&#10;  (Spot instances, 70% cheaper)&#10;&#10;MESSAGE:&#10;{videoId, courseId, lessonId,&#10; s3Key, fileSize}&#10;&#10;FLOW: instructor uploads to S3&#10;via presigned URL → S3 event →&#10;Lambda → Kafka → Spot worker&#10;consumes → FFmpeg 10-15 min&#10;transcode 4 resolutions → HLS&#10;packaging → upload S3 → UPDATE&#10;lessons video_url" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#ef6c00;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="690" width="360" height="220" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="kafkaProgress" value="TOPIC: video.progress&#10;&#10;PRODUCER: User Progress Svc&#10;CONSUMER: user_tracking_consumer_svc&#10;  (10 instances)&#10;PARTITIONS: 100 (by user_id)&#10;&#10;MESSAGE:&#10;{courseId, lessonId, videoId,&#10; position:140, action:WATCHING}&#10;&#10;FLOW: client batches 3 heartbeats&#10;(30 sec) → POST /progress/events&#10;→ Progress Svc publishes each →&#10;Kafka 100 partitions → returns&#10;200 OK immediately (async, does&#10;not block video) → consumer upserts&#10;last_position_sec=latest,&#10;max_position_sec=GREATEST(&#10;existing, new)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#ef6c00;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="440" y="690" width="380" height="260" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="kafkaPayment" value="TOPIC: payment.completed&#10;&#10;PRODUCER: Payment Svc (on webhook)&#10;CONSUMERS: Enrollment Consumer,&#10;  Permission Sync Svc&#10;&#10;MESSAGE:&#10;{paymentId, userId, courseId,&#10; amount}&#10;&#10;FLOW: Stripe webhook confirms&#10;payment_intent.succeeded → Payment&#10;Svc verifies signature → UPDATE&#10;payments COMPLETED → Kafka publish&#10;→ Enrollment Consumer checks&#10;idempotency then INSERT enrollment&#10;→ Permission Sync Svc INSERT&#10;Access ACTIVE LIFETIME (parallel&#10;consumer, independent of enrollment)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#ef6c00;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="840" y="690" width="380" height="220" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="kafkaCourseCompleted" value="TOPIC: course.completed&#10;&#10;PRODUCER: user_tracking_consumer_svc&#10;CONSUMER: Certificate Consumer&#10;&#10;MESSAGE:&#10;{userId, courseId, enrollmentId,&#10; completedAt}&#10;&#10;FLOW: progress consumer detects&#10;max_position_sec &gt;= duration×0.95&#10;on all lessons → recomputes&#10;completion_status=100% → publishes&#10;course.completed → Certificate&#10;Consumer verifies no duplicate&#10;(idempotency guard) → renders PDF&#10;from template → uploads S3 →&#10;INSERT certificates → notify email" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#ef6c00;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="930" width="1160" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="s3Title" value="S3 BLOB STORAGE (Raw Video + HLS Segments + Certificates | 11 Nines Durability)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#c62828;fillColor=#ffebee;align=left;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;rounded=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1260" y="650" width="1060" height="25" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="s3Structure" value="S3 BUCKET STRUCTURE:&#10;&#10;course-videos-raw/&#10;  courses/{courseId}/lessons/{lessonId}/original.mp4 (up to 5GB)&#10;&#10;course-videos-cdn/&#10;  courses/{courseId}/lessons/{lessonId}/&#10;    master.m3u8 (adaptive bitrate playlist)&#10;    1080p.m3u8 + 1080p_segment_000.ts...&#10;    720p.m3u8 + 720p_segment_000.ts...&#10;    480p.m3u8 + 480p_segment_000.ts...&#10;    360p.m3u8 + 360p_segment_000.ts...&#10;    thumbnails/frame_0s.jpg, frame_5s.jpg, frame_10s.jpg&#10;&#10;certificates/&#10;  {userId}/{courseId}.pdf&#10;&#10;UPLOAD FLOW (Instructor):&#10;1. Media Uploader Svc: s3.generatePresignedUrl(putObject, expires:3600)&#10;2. Client uploads directly to S3 (bypasses server, chunked resumable)&#10;3. S3 PUT event triggers Lambda&#10;4. Lambda publishes Kafka video.uploaded&#10;5. Transcode Worker downloads, FFmpeg processes, uploads HLS output&#10;&#10;LIFECYCLE POLICY:&#10;Raw videos: Standard (0-90 days, source of truth) → Glacier after 90 days&#10;  (80% storage cost savings, 0.004 dollars vs 0.023 dollars per GB)&#10;HLS segments: Standard always (frequently accessed, immutable content-&#10;  addressed URLs, 30-day CDN cache TTL means rarely hit origin directly)&#10;Certificates: Standard (small files, permanent, cheap to store forever)&#10;&#10;WHY S3 FOR VIDEO NOT DATABASE:&#10;Petabytes of content across billions of HLS segments impossible in&#10;PostgreSQL. Object storage optimized for large binary blob storage with&#10;11 nines durability, presigned URLs for direct upload/download bypass&#10;server load entirely, purpose-built for CDN origin pull pattern." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffebee;strokeColor=#c62828;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1260" y="690" width="520" height="440" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="elasticTitle" value="ELASTICSEARCH + REDIS (Course Search | Recommendation Cache)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#f57f17;fillColor=#fff9c4;align=left;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;rounded=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1800" y="650" width="540" height="25" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="elasticIndex" value="INDEX: courses (Elasticsearch)&#10;&#10;FIELDS:&#10;course_id (keyword)&#10;instructor_id (keyword)&#10;title (text with ngram analyzer&#10;  for autocomplete)&#10;description (text, stemming)&#10;category (keyword, faceted filter)&#10;level (keyword)&#10;price (numeric, range filter)&#10;rating (numeric, sort/filter)&#10;&#10;SEARCH QUERY:&#10;machine learning + category=&#10;Programming + price&lt;50 +&#10;rating&gt;=4 → single sub-ms query&#10;&#10;CDC AGGREGATOR PIPELINE:&#10;Course DB changes → CDC stream&#10;→ Elasticsearch indexer&#10;Async, never in hot write path&#10;&#10;REDIS CACHE:&#10;course details: 1h TTL, 90% hit&#10;enrollment check: 24h TTL&#10;recommendations: precomputed&#10;  nightly batch ML job, key&#10;  lookup not live inference&#10;&#10;WHY ELASTICSEARCH NOT SQL LIKE:&#10;SQL LIKE scans 100K rows per&#10;keypress. Inverted index gives&#10;instant ranked results, fuzzy&#10;typo tolerance, faceted filters,&#10;autocomplete all in one query." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#f57f17;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1800" y="690" width="540" height="500" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="failureTitle" value="FAILURE SCENARIOS AND RECOVERY STRATEGIES" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#c62828;fillColor=#ffebee;align=left;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;rounded=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="1160" width="2280" height="25" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="fail1" value="FAILURE 1: Stripe Webhook Lost or Delayed&#10;&#10;SCENARIO: Payment succeeds on Stripe side but the webhook to our&#10;server is lost due to network partition or server downtime&#10;&#10;IMPACT: payments table stuck at status=PENDING indefinitely, student&#10;paid but has no enrollment, no Access row, cannot watch course&#10;&#10;RECOVERY (Layer 4 of 5-layer idempotency):&#10;Polling backup job runs every 5 minutes:&#10;SELECT * FROM payments WHERE status=PENDING&#10;  AND created_at &gt; now() - interval 1 hour&#10;FOR EACH pending_payment:&#10;  Query Stripe API: GET /payment_intents/{id}&#10;  IF status=succeeded on Stripe side:&#10;    UPDATE payments SET status=COMPLETED&#10;    Kafka.send(payment.completed) — same event as webhook path&#10;    Enrollment Consumer processes normally (idempotent either way)&#10;&#10;MAX DELAY: 5 minutes (acceptable UX with in-app polling by client)&#10;&#10;PREVENTION: webhook retry configured on Stripe side (exponential&#10;backoff up to 3 days), but polling backup catches true edge cases" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffebee;strokeColor=#c62828;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="1200" width="560" height="360" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="fail2" value="FAILURE 2: Transcode Worker Crash Mid-Processing&#10;&#10;SCENARIO: Spot instance running FFmpeg transcode gets reclaimed by&#10;AWS (2-minute warning) at 60% through a 15-minute job&#10;&#10;IMPACT: video.uploaded Kafka message not acknowledged (consumer&#10;offset not committed), lesson stuck at processing_status=PROCESSING&#10;&#10;RECOVERY:&#10;Kafka consumer offset only commits after successful upload of ALL&#10;HLS variants + UPDATE lessons COMPLETED&#10;If worker crashes mid-job: offset never committed, message remains&#10;unacknowledged, another Transcode Worker instance picks up the&#10;same message and restarts the FULL transcode from original.mp4&#10;&#10;IDEMPOTENCY: re-running FFmpeg on same input produces same output,&#10;overwriting partial S3 uploads is safe (deterministic transcode)&#10;&#10;PREVENTION: mix of Spot and On-Demand worker pool (e.g. 80/20 split)&#10;so critical large uploads land on more stable On-Demand capacity,&#10;checkpoint progress every resolution completed to resume partial work" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#ef6c00;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="640" y="1200" width="560" height="360" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="fail3" value="FAILURE 3: Progress Consumer Lag Under Peak Load&#10;&#10;SCENARIO: Major course launch drives 1M concurrent viewers, video.&#10;progress Kafka topic lag grows beyond 1000 messages per partition&#10;&#10;IMPACT: student's progress updates delayed by minutes, resume&#10;position may show slightly stale data if they close and reopen&#10;quickly, completion certificate generation delayed&#10;&#10;VISIBLE TO USER:&#10;Video playback itself is UNAFFECTED (progress writes are async and&#10;decoupled from playback via Kafka) — only the resume-position and&#10;completion percentage lag behind by the consumer backlog duration&#10;&#10;RECOVERY:&#10;Auto-scaling: user_tracking_consumer_svc scales out when Kafka&#10;consumer lag exceeds 1000 messages (add more of the 10 instances)&#10;100 partitions allow linear horizontal scaling up to 100 consumers&#10;Consumers catch up processing backlog once scaled, GREATEST() upsert&#10;logic means out-of-order catch-up processing still converges correctly&#10;&#10;PREVENTION: pre-scale consumer pool ahead of known course launch&#10;events, monitor partition lag with alerting threshold at 500 messages" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1220" y="1200" width="560" height="360" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="fail4" value="FAILURE 4: CDN Cache Miss Storm (Cold Start)&#10;&#10;SCENARIO: A brand new course goes viral instantly, thousands of&#10;students request the same never-before-cached HLS segments&#10;simultaneously from a CloudFront edge that has zero cache entries&#10;&#10;IMPACT: cache miss triggers origin fetch to S3 (~200ms) for every&#10;single concurrent request instead of the usual sub-50ms cache hit,&#10;temporary spike in S3 GET request volume and origin bandwidth&#10;&#10;RECOVERY:&#10;CloudFront request collapsing: multiple simultaneous cache misses&#10;for the identical object are collapsed into a single origin fetch,&#10;all waiting clients served from that one S3 response once it returns&#10;First request populates edge cache with 30-day TTL, all subsequent&#10;requests (even milliseconds later) hit the now-warm cache&#10;&#10;PREVENTION:&#10;Pre-warming for known high-traffic launches: proactively request&#10;segments from each expected edge region before public announcement&#10;Origin Shield (an additional CloudFront caching layer) reduces&#10;origin load further by deduplicating requests across edge locations" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#f57f17;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1800" y="1200" width="540" height="360" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="fail5" value="FAILURE 5: Certificate Consumer Crashes and Kafka Redelivers Event&#10;&#10;SCENARIO: course.completed event is published, Certificate Consumer&#10;begins rendering the PDF, then the pod crashes before committing&#10;the Kafka consumer offset — Kafka redelivers the same event to a&#10;new consumer instance&#10;&#10;IMPACT: without a safeguard, the student would receive TWO identical&#10;certificates in their inbox and TWO rows in the certificates table&#10;&#10;RECOVERY (idempotency guard):&#10;New consumer instance receives the redelivered course.completed event&#10;SELECT COUNT(*) FROM certificates WHERE user_id=? AND course_id=?&#10;IF count &gt; 0: SKIP entirely, do not re-render or re-email&#10;IF count = 0: proceed normally with generation&#10;&#10;GRACEFUL DEGRADATION:&#10;If the entire Certificate Consumer service is down when a course&#10;completes, the completion flow itself is NOT blocked — the student&#10;still sees Course Completed immediately, with a Your certificate&#10;will be emailed shortly message. The course.completed event stays&#10;in Kafka until a consumer recovers and processes it whenever the&#10;service comes back online — no completion data is ever lost" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffebee;strokeColor=#c62828;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="1580" width="1160" height="380" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="fail6" value="FAILURE 6: PostgreSQL Read Replica Lag Shows Stale Enrollment Count&#10;&#10;SCENARIO: 1 master + 5 read replicas topology, replication lag spikes&#10;to 3 seconds during a traffic surge, course listing page (served from&#10;a read replica) shows students_enrolled count that is a few seconds&#10;stale compared to the master&#10;&#10;IMPACT: minor, cosmetic — a course might show 4,998 enrolled&#10;students when the true count is 5,001 for a few seconds&#10;&#10;WHY THIS IS ACCEPTABLE (CAP tradeoff explicit):&#10;Course catalog and listings are AP (Availability over Consistency) —&#10;this is precisely the tradeoff the system is designed around, stale&#10;enrollment counts by a few seconds are a non-issue for browsing&#10;&#10;CRITICAL DISTINCTION: this same lag tolerance does NOT apply to the&#10;Access table check during video playback (CP path) — that specific&#10;read always goes to the master or a synchronously-replicated replica&#10;to avoid granting playback to a student whose refund was JUST&#10;processed moments ago on the master&#10;&#10;RECOVERY: monitoring alerts if replication lag exceeds 5 seconds&#10;sustained, auto-scaling adds read replicas under sustained high load" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1260" y="1580" width="1080" height="380" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="scaleNote" value="SCALE SUMMARY: 100K+ courses, millions of enrolled students globally, billions of HLS segments in S3, petabytes of content, millions of video requests per day, thousands of enrollments per hour, video startup under 2 sec, 1 PostgreSQL master + 5 read replicas, Progress DB sharded by user_id, Payments sharded by created_at, Kafka 100 partitions by user_id 100K events/sec (10K per consumer times 10 consumers), Redis 90% hit rate 10x DB load reduction, CDN 95% cache hit under 50ms latency, S3 lifecycle 80% storage cost savings after 90-day Glacier transition" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#1976d2;fillColor=#e3f2fd;align=center;fontSize=11;rounded=1;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="1980" width="2280" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
</root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>
